The incoming serdev chunk is appended to the fixed-size `rx_buffer` without checking whether the cumulative data exceeds the buffer capacity. Since the helper can retain leftover bytes and receive multiple packets per callback, this can cause a buffer overflow.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (count > sizeof(bg->rx_buffer) - bg->rx_buffer_len) {
    dev_err_ratelimited(&bg->sd->dev, "Bootloader RX buffer overflow");
    bg->rx_buffer_len = 0;
